    "id": "topic-1789929738805",
    "category": "Python Basics",
    "title": "Output",
    "content": "<p class=\"text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">In Python, the <code>print()</code> function is used to output text, numbers, or variables to the console screen.</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">1. Basic Printing & Formatting</h2>\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400\">Display text strings, multiple arguments, and formatted values using f-strings:</p>\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code># Basic string output\nprint(\"Hello, World!\")\n\n# Printing multiple items separated by space\nname = \"Alice\"\nage = 25\nprint(\"Name:\", name, \"Age:\", age)\n\n# Formatted string (f-string) - Preferred modern method\nprint(f\"User {name} is {age} years old.\")</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">2. Print Parameters (`end` and `sep`)</h2>\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400\">Customize line endings and item separators:</p>\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code># Change separator from space to hyphen\nprint(\"2026\", \"09\", \"20\", sep=\"-\")  # Output: 2026-09-20\n\n# Prevent newline at the end of output\nprint(\"Loading...\", end=\"\")\nprint(\"Done!\")  # Output: Loading...Done!</code></pre>\n</div>\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "topic-1789930976794",
    "category": "Python Basics",
    "title": "comments",
    "content": "<p class=\"text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">Comments explain Python code, make it more readable, and prevent code execution when testing.</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Single-Line & Multi-Line Comments</h2>\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code># This is a single-line comment\n\nx = 10  # Inline comment explaining variable initialization\n\n# Multi-line comments can be written using multiple hash tags:\n# Step 1: Initialize variables\n# Step 2: Compute results\n# Step 3: Print summary\n\n\"\"\"\nMulti-line string literals (triple quotes) are often \nused as documentation strings (docstrings) or \nmulti-line comments when not assigned to a variable.\n\"\"\"</code></pre>\n</div>\n"
  },
