    "id": "topic-1789931342267",
    "category": "Python Basics",
    "title": "variables",
    "content": "<p class=\"text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">Variables are containers for storing data values. In Python, variables are created automatically when you assign a value using the <code>=</code> operator.</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">1. Assigning & Naming Variables</h2>\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code># Creating variables\nport = 8080            # Integer\ntarget_host = \"10.0.0.1\" # String\nis_active = True       # Boolean\n\n# Dynamic typing: variable type changes based on value\ndata = 100\ndata = \"Now a string\"  # Valid in Python</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">2. Multiple Assignments & Conventions</h2>\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code># Assign multiple variables at once\nx, y, z = \"Apple\", \"Banana\", \"Cherry\"\n\n# Assign same value to multiple variables\na = b = c = 0\n\n# Python Naming Convention: snake_case for variables\nmax_connection_attempts = 5</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-950/40 border-l-4 border-amber-500 text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation\"></i> Variable Naming Rules:</strong>\n    Variable names must start with a letter or underscore, cannot start with a number, are case-sensitive (<code>age</code> vs <code>AGE</code>), and cannot be Python keywords (like <code>class</code>, <code>if</code>, <code>for</code>).\n</div>\n\n\n4. Python Data Types\n\n<p class=\"text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">Python has several built-in data types categorized into numbers, text, sequences, mappings, sets, and booleans.</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Core Built-in Data Types</h2>\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code># Text Type\ntext = \"Hello World\"          # str\n\n# Numeric Types\nnum_int = 42                  # int\nnum_float = 3.14159           # float\nnum_complex = 1j              # complex\n\n# Sequence Types\nitems_list = [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"]  # list (mutable, ordered)\nitems_tuple = (\"a\", \"b\", \"c\") # tuple (immutable, ordered)\nnum_range = range(6)          # range\n\n# Mapping Type\nuser_dict = {\"name\": \"Alice\", \"role\": \"Admin\"} # dict\n\n# Set Types\nunique_ports = {80, 443, 22}  # set (unique, unordered)\n\n# Boolean Type\nis_valid = True               # bool\n\n# Binary / None Types\nnothing = None                # NoneType</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Checking Data Types</h2>\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400\">Use the <code>type()</code> function to inspect the data type of any object:</p>\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code>val = 100\nprint(type(val))  # Output: <class 'int'>\n\ndata = [1, 2, 3]\nprint(type(data)) # Output: <class 'list'></code></pre>\n</div>\n\n\n5. Python Numbers\n\n<p class=\"text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">There are three numerical types in Python: <code>int</code>, <code>float</code>, and <code>complex</code>.</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">1. Number Types Overview</h2>\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code># Integers (Whole numbers positive or negative)\na = 10\nb = -8593\nc = 1000000000000000000\n\n# Floats (Floating point numbers containing decimals or scientific notation)\nx = 10.5\ny = -35.82\nz = 35e3 # Scientific float (35000.0)\n\n# Complex numbers (written with a 'j' as the imaginary part)\nc1 = 3 + 5j\nc2 = 5j</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">2. Basic Mathematical Operations</h2>\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code>x = 15\ny = 4\n\nprint(x + y)  # Addition: 19\nprint(x - y)  # Subtraction: 11\nprint(x * y)  # Multiplication: 60\nprint(x / y)  # Division (always returns float): 3.75\nprint(x // y) # Floor Division (discards remainder): 3\nprint(x % y)  # Modulus (returns remainder): 3\nprint(x ** y) # Exponentiation (15^4): 50625</code></pre>\n</div>\n"
  },
