    "id": "topic-1789931552745",
    "category": "Python Basics",
    "title": "Data Types",
    "content": "<p class=\"text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    In Python, a <strong>data type</strong> tells you what kind of value a variable contains. Different data types are designed for different kinds of data and can be used in different ways.\n</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Built-in Data Types</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-3 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Python has several built-in data types. They can be grouped into different categories:\n</p>\n\n<ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <li><code>str</code> — Text</li>\n    <li><code>int</code>, <code>float</code>, <code>complex</code> — Numbers</li>\n    <li><code>list</code>, <code>tuple</code>, <code>range</code> — Sequence types</li>\n    <li><code>dict</code> — Mapping type</li>\n    <li><code>set</code>, <code>frozenset</code> — Set types</li>\n    <li><code>bool</code> — Boolean type</li>\n    <li><code>bytes</code>, <code>bytearray</code>, <code>memoryview</code> — Binary types</li>\n    <li><code>NoneType</code> — Represents <code>None</code></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">1. Text Type — str</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>str</code> type is used for storing text. Strings can be written using single or double quotation marks.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>name = \"Michael\"\nmessage = 'Hello World'\n\nprint(name)\nprint(message)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">2. Numeric Types</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-3 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Python has three main numeric types: <code>int</code>, <code>float</code>, and <code>complex</code>.\n</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">int</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>int</code> represents whole numbers without a decimal point.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>age = 15\nscore = 100\ntemperature = -5</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">float</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>float</code> represents numbers containing a decimal point.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>price = 19.99\nheight = 1.75\ntemperature = -3.5</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">complex</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>complex</code> numbers contain a real part and an imaginary part. Python uses <code>j</code> for the imaginary part.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>x = 3 + 5j\nprint(x)</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">3. Sequence Types</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-3 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Python's sequence types include <code>list</code>, <code>tuple</code>, and <code>range</code>.\n</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">list</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A list stores multiple items in an ordered collection.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">tuple</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A tuple is also an ordered collection, but its contents cannot normally be changed after creation.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\")\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">range</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A <code>range</code> represents a sequence of numbers and is commonly used with loops.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>numbers = range(6)\n\nfor number in numbers:\nprint(number)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-950/40 border-l-4 border-amber-500 text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Remember:\n    </strong>\n    <code>range(6)</code> produces the numbers from <code>0</code> up to, but not including, <code>6</code>.\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">4. Mapping Type — dict</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A dictionary, or <code>dict</code>, stores data as key-value pairs.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>person = {\n    \"name\": \"John\",\n    \"age\": 36\n}\n\nprint(person[\"name\"])\nprint(person[\"age\"])</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Dictionaries are useful when each value needs a meaningful key.\n</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">5. Set Types</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-3 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Python provides <code>set</code> and <code>frozenset</code>.\n</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">set</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A set is an unordered collection of unique values.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">frozenset</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A <code>frozenset</code> is an immutable version of a set.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = frozenset({\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"})\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">6. Boolean Type — bool</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>bool</code> type can have one of two values: <code>True</code> or <code>False</code>.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>is_logged_in = True\nhas_permission = False\n\nprint(is_logged_in)\nprint(has_permission)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-shield-halved\"></i> Cybersecurity Connection:\n    </strong>\n    Boolean values are commonly used for security checks, such as determining whether a user is authenticated or whether access has been granted.\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">7. Binary Types</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-3 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Python has three binary data types: <code>bytes</code>, <code>bytearray</code>, and <code>memoryview</code>.\n</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">bytes</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>bytes</code> type is used for binary data and is immutable.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>data = b\"Hello\"\n\nprint(data)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">bytearray</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>bytearray</code> is similar to <code>bytes</code>, but it can be modified.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>data = bytearray(5)\n\nprint(data)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">memoryview</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>memoryview</code> provides access to the memory of another binary object without copying the data.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>data = memoryview(bytes(5))\n\nprint(data)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">8. None Type — NoneType</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>None</code> represents the absence of a value. Its data type is <code>NoneType</code>.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>result = None\n\nprint(result)\nprint(type(result))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Checking a Data Type</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    You can find the data type of an object using Python's <code>type()</code> function.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>x = 5\n\nprint(type(x))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The output will show the type of the value stored in <code>x</code>.\n</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Python Chooses the Data Type</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-3 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    In Python, a variable gets its data type when you assign a value to it.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>x = \"Hello World\"       # str\nx = 20                    # int\nx = 20.5                  # float\nx = 1j                    # complex\nx = [\"apple\", \"banana\"]   # list\nx = (\"apple\", \"banana\")   # tuple\nx = range(6)              # range\nx = {\"name\": \"John\"}      # dict\nx = {\"apple\", \"banana\"}   # set\nx = frozenset({\"apple\", \"banana\"})\nx = True                  # bool\nx = b\"Hello\"              # bytes\nx = bytearray(5)          # bytearray\nx = memoryview(bytes(5))  # memoryview\nx = None                  # NoneType</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Specifying a Data Type</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-3 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Python also provides constructor functions that can be used to explicitly create specific data types.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>x = str(\"Hello World\")\nx = int(20)\nx = float(20.5)\nx = complex(1j)\n\nx = list((\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"))\nx = tuple((\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"))\nx = range(6)\n\nx = dict(name=\"John\", age=36)\n\nx = set((\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"))\nx = frozenset((\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"))\n\nx = bool(5)\n\nx = bytes(5)\nx = bytearray(5)\nx = memoryview(bytes(5))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Key Idea:\n    </strong>\n    The value you assign to a variable determines its type. Use <code>type()</code> when you need to check what type an object is.\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Quick Reference</h2>\n\n<div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n    <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse\">\n        <thead>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-700\">\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Type</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Example</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Purpose</th>\n            </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>str</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>\"Hello\"</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Text</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>int</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>10</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Whole numbers</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>float</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>10.5</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Decimal numbers</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>complex</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>2j</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Complex numbers</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>list</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>[1, 2, 3]</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Ordered collection</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>tuple</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>(1, 2, 3)</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Ordered collection</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>range</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>range(5)</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Sequence of numbers</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>dict</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>{\"age\": 15}</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Key-value data</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>set</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>{1, 2, 3}</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Unique values</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>frozenset</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>frozenset({1, 2})</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Immutable set</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>bool</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>True</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">True/False values</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>bytes</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>b\"Hi\"</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Binary data</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>bytearray</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>bytearray(5)</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Mutable binary data</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>memoryview</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>memoryview(bytes(5))</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">View of binary memory</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>NoneType</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>None</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">No value</td>\n            </tr>\n        </tbody>\n    </table>\n</div>\n"
  },
