    "id": "topic-1789934750771",
    "category": "Python Basics",
    "title": "Boolean",
    "content": "<p class=\"text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Booleans are a Python data type that can have one of two values:\n    <code>True</code> or <code>False</code>.\n    Boolean values are commonly used when a program needs to determine whether something is true or false.\n</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Boolean Values</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Python can evaluate expressions and return either <code>True</code> or <code>False</code>.\n    Comparisons between values produce Boolean results.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>print(10 > 9)\nprint(10 == 9)\nprint(10 < 9)</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The results are:\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n    <pre><code>True\nFalse\nFalse</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Booleans in if Statements</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Conditions in an <code>if</code> statement are evaluated as <code>True</code> or <code>False</code>.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>a = 200\nb = 33\n\nif b > a:\nprint(\"b is greater than a\")\nelse:\nprint(\"b is not greater than a\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Key Idea:\n    </strong>\n    A condition does not have to be stored in a Boolean variable first.\n    Python can evaluate the condition directly.\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Evaluating Values and Variables</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>bool()</code> function evaluates a value and returns either <code>True</code> or <code>False</code>.\n</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Evaluate a String and a Number</h3>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>print(bool(\"Hello\"))\nprint(bool(15))</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Both values contain information, so they evaluate to <code>True</code>.\n</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Evaluate Variables</h3>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>x = \"Hello\"\ny = 15\n\nprint(bool(x))\nprint(bool(y))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Most Values Are True</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Most Python values evaluate to <code>True</code> when they contain some sort of content.\n</p>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Non-empty strings evaluate to <code>True</code>.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>print(bool(\"Hello\"))</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Non-zero numbers evaluate to <code>True</code>.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>print(bool(15))\nprint(bool(-5))</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Non-empty lists, tuples, sets, and dictionaries also evaluate to <code>True</code>.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>print(bool([\"apple\", \"cherry\", \"banana\"]))\nprint(bool((\"apple\", \"banana\")))\nprint(bool({\"apple\", \"banana\"}))\nprint(bool({\"name\": \"John\"}))</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Remember:\n    </strong>\n    Values that contain data are generally considered <code>True</code>.\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Some Values Are False</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Python has a small set of commonly encountered values that evaluate to <code>False</code>.\n    These include empty collections, an empty string, the number <code>0</code>, <code>None</code>,\n    and <code>False</code> itself.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>print(bool(False))\nprint(bool(None))\nprint(bool(0))\nprint(bool(\"\"))\nprint(bool(()))\nprint(bool([]))\nprint(bool({}))</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-950/40 border-l-4 border-amber-500 text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation\"></i> Important:\n    </strong>\n    An empty string, empty list, empty tuple, empty set, and empty dictionary are all\n    considered <code>False</code> when converted to a Boolean.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">The Value 0</h3>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>number = 0\n\nprint(bool(number))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">The Value None</h3>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>value = None\n\nprint(bool(value))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Custom Objects Can Be False</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    An object created from a class can evaluate to <code>False</code> when its\n    <code>__len__()</code> method returns <code>0</code> or <code>False</code>.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>class MyClass:\n    def __len__(self):\n        return 0\n\nmyobj = MyClass()\n\nprint(bool(myobj))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Since <code>__len__()</code> returns <code>0</code>, the object evaluates to <code>False</code>.\n</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Functions Can Return a Boolean</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A function can return a Boolean value just like it can return any other type of value.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>def myFunction():\n    return True\n\nprint(myFunction())</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Using the Function as a Condition</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The Boolean result returned by a function can be used directly in an <code>if</code> statement.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>def myFunction():\n    return True\n\nif myFunction():\nprint(\"YES!\")\nelse:\nprint(\"NO!\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Useful Pattern:\n    </strong>\n    Functions that answer questions can return <code>True</code> or <code>False</code>,\n    making them useful directly inside conditions.\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">isinstance() Returns a Boolean</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Python has many built-in functions that return Boolean values.\n    One useful example is <code>isinstance()</code>, which checks whether an object\n    is an instance of a specified data type.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>x = 200\n\nprint(isinstance(x, int))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Since <code>x</code> is an integer, the result is <code>True</code>.\n</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Checking Different Types</h3>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>x = \"Hello\"\n\nprint(isinstance(x, str))\nprint(isinstance(x, int))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Truth Values Quick Reference</h2>\n\n<div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n    <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse\">\n        <thead>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-700\">\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Value</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">bool(value)</th>\n            </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>True</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>True</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>False</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>False</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>0</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>False</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>1</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>True</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>\"\"</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>False</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>\"Hello\"</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>True</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>[]</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>False</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>[1, 2]</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>True</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>{}</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>False</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>{\"name\": \"John\"}</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>True</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>None</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>False</code></td>\n            </tr>\n        </tbody>\n    </table>\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Boolean Examples</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Boolean values are especially useful when a program needs to make a decision.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>username = \"admin\"\n\nprint(username == \"admin\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>age = 18\n\nif age >= 18:\nprint(\"Access allowed\")\nelse:\nprint(\"Access denied\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-shield-halved\"></i> Cybersecurity Connection:\n    </strong>\n    Boolean logic is fundamental to security programs because checks such as authentication,\n    authorisation, validation, and access control often depend on conditions that evaluate to\n    <code>True</code> or <code>False</code>.\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Key Takeaways</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <li>Python Boolean values are <code>True</code> and <code>False</code>.</li>\n    <li>Comparisons and conditions produce Boolean results.</li>\n    <li><code>bool()</code> converts a value into <code>True</code> or <code>False</code>.</li>\n    <li>Most non-empty and non-zero values are truthy.</li>\n    <li>Empty values, <code>0</code>, <code>None</code>, and <code>False</code> are commonly falsy.</li>\n    <li>Functions can return Boolean values.</li>\n    <li><code>isinstance()</code> returns a Boolean indicating whether an object matches a specified type.</li>\n</ul>\n"
