    "id": "topic-1790008660168",
    "category": "Python Basics",
    "title": "Lists",
    "content": "<p class=\"text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Lists are used to store multiple items in a single variable. A Python list is created using\n    square brackets <code>[]</code>.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">List Characteristics</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-3 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Python lists have several important characteristics.\n</p>\n\n<ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <li>Lists are ordered.</li>\n    <li>Lists are changeable.</li>\n    <li>Lists allow duplicate values.</li>\n    <li>List items are indexed starting from <code>0</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Ordered</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Items in a list have a defined order. That order normally remains the same unless you use\n    an operation that changes it, such as sorting or reversing the list.\n</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Changeable</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Lists are mutable, which means their contents can be changed after the list has been created.\n    Items can be changed, added, and removed.\n</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Allow Duplicates</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A list can contain the same value more than once.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\", \"apple\", \"cherry\"]\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">List Length</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Use <code>len()</code> to find how many items a list contains.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nprint(len(fruits))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">List Item Data Types</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    List items can be any Python data type.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>strings = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\nnumbers = [1, 5, 7, 9, 3]\nbooleans = [True, False, False]</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A single list can also contain different data types.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>items = [\"abc\", 34, True, 40, \"male\"]\n\nprint(items)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Checking the List Type</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Use <code>type()</code> to check the type of an object.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nprint(type(fruits))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">The list() Constructor</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    You can also create a list using the <code>list()</code> constructor.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = list((\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"))\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-950/40 border-l-4 border-amber-500 text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Note:\n    </strong>\n    When passing several values to <code>list()</code>, the values are commonly supplied through\n    another iterable such as a tuple.\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Access List Items</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    List items are accessed using their index inside square brackets. Python starts indexing at <code>0</code>.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nprint(fruits[0])\nprint(fruits[1])\nprint(fruits[2])</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Negative Indexing</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Negative indexes count from the end of the list. <code>-1</code> refers to the last item,\n    <code>-2</code> to the second-last item, and so on.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nprint(fruits[-1])\nprint(fruits[-2])</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Range of Indexes</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A range can be selected with <code>start:end</code>. The start index is included, while the end\n    index is not included.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\", \"orange\", \"kiwi\", \"melon\", \"mango\"]\n\nprint(fruits[2:5])</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    You can leave out the start or end index.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\", \"orange\", \"kiwi\", \"melon\", \"mango\"]\n\nprint(fruits[:4])\nprint(fruits[2:])</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Ranges with Negative Indexes</h3>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\", \"orange\", \"kiwi\", \"melon\", \"mango\"]\n\nprint(fruits[-4:-1])</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Check if an Item Exists</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>in</code> keyword checks whether an item exists in a list.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nif \"apple\" in fruits:\nprint(\"Apple is in the list\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Change List Items</h2>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Change a Single Item</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Assign a new value to a specific index to replace an existing item.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nfruits[1] = \"blackcurrant\"\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Change a Range of Items</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A slice can be replaced with another list. The number of new items does not have to match the\n    number of items being replaced, so the length of the list can change.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nfruits[1:3] = [\"blackcurrant\", \"watermelon\"]\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Replacing fewer items than the slice contains makes the list shorter.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nfruits[1:3] = [\"watermelon\"]\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Replacing fewer positions with more items makes the list longer.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nfruits[1:2] = [\"blackcurrant\", \"watermelon\"]\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Insert Without Replacing</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Use <code>insert()</code> when you want to add an item at a particular position without replacing\n    the existing item.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nfruits.insert(2, \"watermelon\")\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Add List Items</h2>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">append()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>append()</code> adds one item to the end of the list.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nfruits.append(\"orange\")\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">insert()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>insert(index, value)</code> places a new item at a specified position.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nfruits.insert(1, \"orange\")\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">extend()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>extend()</code> adds the elements from another iterable to the end of the current list.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\ntropical = [\"mango\", \"pineapple\", \"papaya\"]\n\nfruits.extend(tropical)\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The iterable supplied to <code>extend()</code> does not have to be a list. It can also be a\n    tuple, set, or another iterable.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\nmore_fruits = (\"kiwi\", \"orange\")\n\nfruits.extend(more_fruits)\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Remove List Items</h2>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">remove()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>remove()</code> removes the first occurrence of a specified value.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\", \"banana\"]\n\nfruits.remove(\"banana\")\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">pop()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>pop(index)</code> removes an item at a specified position. Without an index,\n    <code>pop()</code> removes the last item.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nfruits.pop(1)\n\nprint(fruits)\n\nfruits.pop()\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">del</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>del</code> keyword can remove an item at a specified index.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\ndel fruits[0]\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>del</code> can also delete the entire list.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\ndel fruits</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">clear()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>clear()</code> removes all items from the list but leaves the list itself in place.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nfruits.clear()\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Loop Through a List</h2>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Using a for Loop</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A <code>for</code> loop can visit each item in a list.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nfor fruit in fruits:\nprint(fruit)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Loop Through Index Numbers</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>range()</code> and <code>len()</code> can be used to loop through the indexes.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nfor i in range(len(fruits)):\nprint(fruits[i])</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Using a while Loop</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A <code>while</code> loop can also move through a list by using an index. The index must be\n    increased so that the loop eventually ends.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\ni = 0\n\nwhile i < len(fruits):\nprint(fruits[i])\ni += 1</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Loop Using List Comprehension</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    List comprehension can provide a compact way to perform an operation for every item.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\n[print(x) for x in fruits]</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">List Comprehension</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    List comprehension provides a compact way to create a new list from an existing iterable.\n</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Without List Comprehension</h3>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\", \"kiwi\", \"mango\"]\n\nnewlist = []\n\nfor fruit in fruits:\nif \"a\" in fruit:\nnewlist.append(fruit)\n\nprint(newlist)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">With List Comprehension</h3>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\", \"kiwi\", \"mango\"]\n\nnewlist = [fruit for fruit in fruits if \"a\" in fruit]\n\nprint(newlist)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">List Comprehension Syntax</h3>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>newlist = [expression for item in iterable if condition]</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The condition is optional. Without a condition, every item can be included.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nnewlist = [x for x in fruits]\n\nprint(newlist)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Conditions as Filters</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The condition determines which items are accepted into the new list.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nnewlist = [x for x in fruits if x != \"apple\"]\n\nprint(newlist)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Using range()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The iterable can be something other than a list, such as the sequence produced by <code>range()</code>.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>numbers = [x for x in range(10)]\n\nprint(numbers)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A condition can be added to the range.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>numbers = [x for x in range(10) if x &lt; 5]\n\nprint(numbers)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Expressions</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The expression controls what value is placed into the new list. It can transform the current item.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nnewlist = [x.upper() for x in fruits]\n\nprint(newlist)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The expression can also produce the same value for every item.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nnewlist = [\"hello\" for x in fruits]\n\nprint(newlist)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Conditional Expression</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A conditional expression can change the value placed into the new list.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\nnewlist = [x if x != \"banana\" else \"orange\" for x in fruits]\n\nprint(newlist)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Sort Lists</h2>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Alphanumerical Sorting</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>sort()</code> sorts list items in ascending order by default.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"orange\", \"mango\", \"kiwi\", \"pineapple\", \"banana\"]\n\nfruits.sort()\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Numbers can also be sorted.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code>numbers = [100, 50, 65, 82, 23]\n\nnumbers.sort()\n\nprint(numbers)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Descending Order</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Use <code>reverse=True</code> with <code>sort()</code> to sort in descending order.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code>numbers = [100, 50, 65, 82, 23]\n\nnumbers.sort(reverse=True)\n\nprint(numbers)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Custom Sort Function</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>key</code> argument allows you to specify a function that determines the value used for sorting.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code>def distance_from_50(number):\n    return abs(number - 50)\n\nnumbers = [100, 50, 65, 82, 23]\n\nnumbers.sort(key=distance_from_50)\n\nprint(numbers)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Case-Insensitive Sorting</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Normal string sorting is case-sensitive. <code>str.lower</code> can be supplied as the key\n    function for a case-insensitive sort.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"banana\", \"Orange\", \"Kiwi\", \"cherry\"]\n\nfruits.sort(key=str.lower)\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Reverse the Current Order</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>reverse()</code> method reverses the current order of the items.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"banana\", \"Orange\", \"Kiwi\", \"cherry\"]\n\nfruits.reverse()\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Copy Lists</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Assigning one list variable directly to another does not create an independent copy.\n    Both variables refer to the same list object.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>list1 = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\nlist2 = list1\n\nlist1.append(\"orange\")\n\nprint(list1)\nprint(list2)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">copy()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>copy()</code> method creates a separate list.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code>list1 = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\nlist2 = list1.copy()\n\nprint(list2)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">list()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>list()</code> constructor can also be used to create a copy.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code>list1 = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\nlist2 = list(list1)\n\nprint(list2)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Slice Operator</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A full slice can also create a new list.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code>list1 = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\nlist2 = list1[:]\n\nprint(list2)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Join Lists</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Python provides several ways to combine two or more lists.\n</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Using +</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>+</code> operator creates a new list containing the items from both lists.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code>list1 = [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"]\nlist2 = [1, 2, 3]\n\nlist3 = list1 + list2\n\nprint(list3)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Using a for Loop</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Items from one list can also be appended to another one by looping through them.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code>list1 = [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"]\nlist2 = [1, 2, 3]\n\nfor item in list2:\nlist1.append(item)\n\nprint(list1)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Using extend()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>extend()</code> adds the items from one list to another.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code>list1 = [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"]\nlist2 = [1, 2, 3]\n\nlist1.extend(list2)\n\nprint(list1)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">List Methods</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-3 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Python provides built-in methods for working with lists.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n    <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse\">\n        <thead>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-700\">\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Method</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Purpose</th>\n            </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>append()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Adds an item to the end of the list.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>clear()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Removes all items from the list.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>copy()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Returns a copy of the list.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>count()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Returns the number of occurrences of a value.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>extend()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Adds items from an iterable to the list.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>index()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Returns the index of the first matching value.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>insert()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Adds an item at a specified position.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>pop()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Removes an item at a specified position.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>remove()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Removes the first matching value.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>reverse()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Reverses the order of the items.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>sort()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Sorts the list.</td>\n            </tr>\n        </tbody>\n    </table>\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Using count()</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>count()</code> tells you how many times a value occurs.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code>numbers = [1, 2, 2, 3, 2]\n\nprint(numbers.count(2))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Using index()</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>index()</code> returns the position of the first matching value.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\", \"banana\"]\n\nprint(fruits.index(\"banana\"))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Lists and Cybersecurity</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Lists are especially useful in cybersecurity programming because security tools frequently\n    need to store groups of values such as IP addresses, ports, file names, log entries,\n    usernames, URLs, or results from a scan.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n    <pre><code>open_ports = [22, 80, 443, 8080]\n\nfor port in open_ports:\nprint(f\"Open port: {port}\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-shield-halved\"></i> Cybersecurity Connection:\n    </strong>\n    Lists can be used to collect and process security-related data before it is searched,\n    filtered, sorted, compared, or written to a file.\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Quick Reference</h2>\n\n<div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n    <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse\">\n        <thead>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-700\">\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Task</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Python</th>\n            </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Create</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>items = [1, 2, 3]</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Access</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>items[0]</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Negative index</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>items[-1]</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Slice</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>items[1:4]</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Length</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>len(items)</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Change</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>items[0] = \"new\"</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Add to end</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>items.append(x)</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Insert</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>items.insert(1, x)</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Add many</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>items.extend(other)</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Remove by value</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>items.remove(x)</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Remove by index</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>items.pop(1)</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Clear</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>items.clear()</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Sort</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>items.sort()</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Reverse</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>items.reverse()</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Copy</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>items.copy()</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Count</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>items.count(x)</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Find index</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>items.index(x)</code></td>\n            </tr>\n        </tbody>\n    </table>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 border-l-4 border-slate-500 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold\">Key takeaway:</strong>\n    Lists are ordered, changeable collections that can contain duplicate values.\n    The core skills are accessing, changing, adding, removing, looping, comprehending,\n    sorting, copying, joining, and using list methods.\n</div>\n"
