    "category": "Python Basics",
    "title": "Tuples",
    "content": "<p class=\"text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Tuples are used to store multiple items in a single variable. A tuple is an ordered and\n    unchangeable collection. Tuples are commonly written using round brackets <code>()</code>.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\")\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Tuple Characteristics</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <li>Tuples are ordered.</li>\n    <li>Tuples are unchangeable.</li>\n    <li>Tuples allow duplicate values.</li>\n    <li>Tuple items are indexed starting from <code>0</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Ordered</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    When a tuple is ordered, its items have a defined position. That order does not change.\n</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Unchangeable</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Tuples are immutable. This means you cannot directly change, add, or remove items after the\n    tuple has been created.\n</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Allow Duplicates</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Because tuple items have indexes, the same value can appear more than once.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\", \"apple\", \"cherry\")\n\nprint(fruits)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Creating a Tuple</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The normal way to create a tuple is to place the items inside round brackets.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>thistuple = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\")\n\nprint(thistuple)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Tuple Without Parentheses</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Python can also create a tuple without explicitly writing the round brackets.\n    The commas are what separate the values into a tuple.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>thistuple = \"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"\n\nprint(thistuple)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Tuple Length</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Use <code>len()</code> to find the number of items in a tuple.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>thistuple = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\")\n\nprint(len(thistuple))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Creating a One-Item Tuple</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A tuple containing only one item must have a comma after that item.\n    Without the comma, Python treats the value as the value itself rather than as a tuple.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>one_item = (\"apple\",)\n\nprint(type(one_item))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    This is not a tuple because the comma is missing:\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>not_a_tuple = (\"apple\")\n\nprint(type(not_a_tuple))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-rose-50 dark:bg-rose-950/40 border-l-4 border-rose-500 text-rose-900 dark:text-rose-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation\"></i> Remember:\n    </strong>\n    For a one-item tuple, the <strong>comma</strong> is essential:\n    <code>(\"apple\",)</code>\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Creating an Empty Tuple</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    An empty tuple is created using empty round brackets.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>empty = ()\n\nprint(empty)\nprint(type(empty))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Tuple Item Data Types</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Tuple items can contain any Python data type.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>tuple1 = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\")\ntuple2 = (1, 5, 7, 9, 3)\ntuple3 = (True, False, False)</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A tuple can also contain different data types at the same time.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>mixed = (\"abc\", 34, True, 40, \"male\")\n\nprint(mixed)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Checking the Type</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Use <code>type()</code> to check whether an object is a tuple.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>mytuple = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\")\n\nprint(type(mytuple))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">The tuple() Constructor</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>tuple()</code> constructor creates a tuple from an iterable.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>thistuple = tuple((\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"))\n\nprint(thistuple)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-950/40 border-l-4 border-amber-500 text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Note:\n    </strong>\n    When using the <code>tuple()</code> constructor with several values, W3Schools demonstrates\n    passing an iterable such as another collection.\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Access Tuple Items</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Tuple items are accessed using their index inside square brackets.\n    The first item has index <code>0</code>.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>thistuple = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\")\n\nprint(thistuple[0])\nprint(thistuple[1])\nprint(thistuple[2])</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Negative Indexing</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Negative indexing starts from the end of the tuple.\n    <code>-1</code> refers to the last item and <code>-2</code> refers to the second-last item.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>thistuple = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\")\n\nprint(thistuple[-1])\nprint(thistuple[-2])</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Range of Indexes</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    You can select a range of tuple items using <code>start:end</code>.\n    The start position is included and the end position is excluded.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>thistuple = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\", \"orange\", \"kiwi\", \"melon\", \"mango\")\n\nprint(thistuple[2:5])</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Leaving out the start position begins the slice at the first item.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>print(thistuple[:4])</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Leaving out the end position continues the slice to the end of the tuple.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>print(thistuple[2:])</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Range of Negative Indexes</h3>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>thistuple = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\", \"orange\", \"kiwi\", \"melon\", \"mango\")\n\nprint(thistuple[-4:-1])</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Check if an Item Exists</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Use the <code>in</code> keyword to check whether an item is present in a tuple.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>thistuple = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\")\n\nif \"apple\" in thistuple:\nprint(\"Apple is in the tuple\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Update Tuples</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Tuples cannot be changed directly because they are unchangeable.\n    However, you can work around this by converting the tuple into a list,\n    modifying the list, and then converting it back to a tuple.\n</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Change a Tuple Item</h3>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>thistuple = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\")\n\ntemp = list(thistuple)\ntemp[1] = \"kiwi\"\nthistuple = tuple(temp)\n\nprint(thistuple)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Add an Item</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Convert the tuple to a list, use a list method such as <code>append()</code>,\n    and convert it back into a tuple.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>thistuple = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\")\n\ntemp = list(thistuple)\ntemp.append(\"orange\")\nthistuple = tuple(temp)\n\nprint(thistuple)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Add a Tuple to a Tuple</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    You can use the <code>+</code> operator to combine another tuple with the existing tuple.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>thistuple = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\")\ny = (\"orange\",)\n\nthistuple += y\n\nprint(thistuple)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Remove an Item</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A tuple item cannot be removed directly. Convert the tuple to a list, remove the item,\n    and convert it back.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>thistuple = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\")\n\ntemp = list(thistuple)\ntemp.remove(\"apple\")\nthistuple = tuple(temp)\n\nprint(thistuple)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-950/40 border-l-4 border-amber-500 text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Important:\n    </strong>\n    Converting a tuple to a list does not make the original tuple mutable.\n    You are creating a list, changing that list, and then creating a new tuple.\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Delete a Tuple</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Although you cannot remove individual items from a tuple directly, you can delete the entire\n    tuple using the <code>del</code> keyword.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>thistuple = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\")\n\ndel thistuple</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Unpack a Tuple</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Packing means putting several values into a tuple. Unpacking means extracting those values\n    into separate variables.\n</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Packing</h3>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\")</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Unpacking</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The number of variables normally needs to match the number of values in the tuple.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\")\n\n(green, yellow, red) = fruits\n\nprint(green)\nprint(yellow)\nprint(red)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Using an Asterisk *</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    If there are more tuple values than variables, an asterisk can be placed before one variable.\n    That variable collects the remaining values into a list.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\", \"strawberry\", \"raspberry\")\n\n(green, yellow, *red) = fruits\n\nprint(green)\nprint(yellow)\nprint(red)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The starred variable does not have to be last. Python assigns values to it until enough\n    values remain for the other variables.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = (\"apple\", \"mango\", \"papaya\", \"pineapple\", \"cherry\")\n\n(green, *tropical, red) = fruits\n\nprint(green)\nprint(tropical)\nprint(red)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Loop Through a Tuple</h2>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Using a for Loop</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A <code>for</code> loop can process each item in a tuple.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>thistuple = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\")\n\nfor item in thistuple:\nprint(item)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Loop Through Index Numbers</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>range()</code> and <code>len()</code> can be used to loop through tuple indexes.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>thistuple = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\")\n\nfor i in range(len(thistuple)):\nprint(thistuple[i])</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Using a while Loop</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A <code>while</code> loop can process the tuple by using an index.\n    The index should be increased after every iteration.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>thistuple = (\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\")\n\ni = 0\n\nwhile i < len(thistuple):\nprint(thistuple[i])\ni += 1</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Join Two Tuples</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>+</code> operator can be used to combine two tuples into a new tuple.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>tuple1 = (\"a\", \"b\", \"c\")\ntuple2 = (1, 2, 3)\n\ntuple3 = tuple1 + tuple2\n\nprint(tuple3)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Multiply Tuples</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>*</code> operator repeats the contents of a tuple a specified number of times.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>fruits = (\"apple\", \"banana\")\n\nresult = fruits * 2\n\nprint(result)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Tuple Methods</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-3 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Tuples have two built-in methods provided specifically for working with tuple values:\n    <code>count()</code> and <code>index()</code>.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n    <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse\">\n        <thead>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-700\">\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Method</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Purpose</th>\n            </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>count()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Returns how many times a specified value occurs.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>index()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Finds the first occurrence of a value and returns its position.</td>\n            </tr>\n        </tbody>\n    </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">count()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Use <code>count()</code> to count the occurrences of a value.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>thistuple = (1, 3, 7, 8, 7, 5, 4, 6, 8, 5)\n\nprint(thistuple.count(5))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">index()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>index()</code> method finds the first occurrence of a specified value and returns\n    its position. It can optionally be given a start and end position for the search.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>thistuple = (1, 3, 7, 8, 7, 5, 4, 6, 8, 5)\n\nposition = thistuple.index(8)\n\nprint(position)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">index() with a Start Position</h3>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>thistuple = (1, 3, 7, 8, 7, 5, 4, 6, 8, 5)\n\nposition = thistuple.index(8, 5)\n\nprint(position)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">index() with Start and End</h3>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>thistuple = (1, 3, 7, 8, 7, 5, 4, 6, 8, 5)\n\nposition = thistuple.index(8, 4, 7)\n\nprint(position)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-rose-50 dark:bg-rose-950/40 border-l-4 border-rose-500 text-rose-900 dark:text-rose-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation\"></i> Important:\n    </strong>\n    <code>index()</code> raises an exception when the requested value cannot be found in the tuple.\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Tuple vs List</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-3 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Tuples and lists are both used to store collections of values, but their behaviour is different.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n    <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse\">\n        <thead>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-700\">\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Property</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">List</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Tuple</th>\n            </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Ordered</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Yes</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Yes</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Changeable</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Yes</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">No</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Duplicates</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Allowed</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Allowed</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Common brackets</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>[]</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>()</code></td>\n            </tr>\n        </tbody>\n    </table>\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Tuples and Cybersecurity</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Tuples can be useful when you want to group related values that should not be modified.\n    For example, a program might represent a fixed network endpoint using an IP address and port.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>server = (\"192.168.1.10\", 443)\n\nip = server[0]\nport = server[1]\n\nprint(ip)\nprint(port)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-shield-halved\"></i> Cybersecurity Connection:\n    </strong>\n    Tuples are useful for fixed collections of related values, such as an IP address and port,\n    coordinates, configuration values, or other data that should remain unchanged after creation.\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Quick Reference</h2>\n\n<div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n    <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse\">\n        <thead>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-700\">\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Task</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Python</th>\n            </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Create tuple</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>(\"a\", \"b\", \"c\")</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">One-item tuple</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>(\"a\",)</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Empty tuple</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>()</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Check type</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>type(tuple1)</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Length</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>len(tuple1)</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Access item</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>tuple1[0]</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Negative index</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>tuple1[-1]</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Slice</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>tuple1[1:4]</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Check membership</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>x in tuple1</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Join tuples</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>tuple1 + tuple2</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Repeat tuple</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>tuple1 * 2</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Count value</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>tuple1.count(x)</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Find value</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>tuple1.index(x)</code></td>\n            </tr>\n        </tbody>\n    </table>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 border-l-4 border-slate-500 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold\">Key takeaway:</strong>\n    Tuples are ordered and unchangeable collections. Learn how to create them,\n    access and slice their items, unpack them, loop through them, join them,\n    and use <code>count()</code> and <code>index()</code>.\n</div>\n"
