    "category": "Python Basics",
    "title": "Sets",
    "content": "<p class=\"text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Sets are used to store multiple items in a single variable. A set is a collection that is\n    unordered, unindexed, and does not allow duplicate values. Sets are written using curly\n    brackets <code>{}</code>.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>myset = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\n\nprint(myset)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-950/40 border-l-4 border-amber-500 text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Important:\n    </strong>\n    Sets are unordered, so you should not rely on a particular order when displaying or looping through their items.\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Set Characteristics</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <li>Sets are unordered.</li>\n    <li>Set items cannot be changed after they are added.</li>\n    <li>Sets are unindexed.</li>\n    <li>Sets do not allow duplicate values.</li>\n    <li>Items can be added and removed after the set is created.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Unordered</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    An unordered collection does not have a fixed item position that you can rely on.\n    You cannot use indexes such as <code>myset[0]</code> to access set items.\n</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Unchangeable Items</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Once an item has been placed in a set, that item itself cannot be changed.\n    However, items can be removed and new items can be added.\n</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Duplicates Not Allowed</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A set automatically removes duplicate values.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>myset = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\", \"apple\"}\n\nprint(myset)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Key Idea:\n    </strong>\n    If a value appears more than once, the set keeps only one occurrence.\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">True, False, 1 and 0</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    In sets, <code>True</code> and <code>1</code> are treated as the same value.\n    Likewise, <code>False</code> and <code>0</code> are treated as the same value.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>myset = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\", True, 1, 2}\n\nprint(myset)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>myset = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\", False, True, 0}\n\nprint(myset)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Get the Length of a Set</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Use the <code>len()</code> function to find how many items are in a set.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>myset = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\n\nprint(len(myset))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Set Item Data Types</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Set items can contain different Python data types.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>set1 = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\nset2 = {1, 5, 7, 9, 3}\nset3 = {True, False, False}\n\nprint(set1)\nprint(set2)\nprint(set3)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A set can also contain a mixture of different types.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>myset = {\"abc\", 34, True, 40, \"male\"}\n\nprint(myset)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Check the Type of a Set</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Python identifies sets using the <code>set</code> data type.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>myset = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\n\nprint(type(myset))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">The set() Constructor</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    You can create a set using the <code>set()</code> constructor. It accepts an iterable such as\n    a list, tuple, or string.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>myset = set((\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"))\n\nprint(myset)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The double round brackets occur because the tuple is being passed as the argument to\n    <code>set()</code>.\n</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Access Set Items</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    You cannot access set items by using an index or key because sets are unindexed.\n    Instead, you can loop through the set or check whether a value exists.\n</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Loop Through a Set</h3>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>myset = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\n\nfor item in myset:\nprint(item)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Check if an Item Exists</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Use the <code>in</code> keyword to check whether a value is present.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>myset = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\n\nprint(\"banana\" in myset)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Check if an Item Does NOT Exist</h3>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>myset = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\n\nprint(\"orange\" not in myset)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Add Set Items</h2>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">add()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Use <code>add()</code> to add one element to a set. If that value is already present,\n    the set remains unchanged.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>myset = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\n\nmyset.add(\"orange\")\n\nprint(myset)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">update()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Use <code>update()</code> to add multiple elements from another iterable.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>myset = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\ntropical = {\"pineapple\", \"mango\", \"papaya\"}\n\nmyset.update(tropical)\n\nprint(myset)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The iterable supplied to <code>update()</code> can be a list, tuple, dictionary, another set,\n    or another iterable.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>myset = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\nmylist = [\"kiwi\", \"orange\"]\n\nmyset.update(mylist)\n\nprint(myset)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Remove Set Items</h2>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">remove()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>remove()</code> deletes a specified element. It raises an error if the element does not exist.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>myset = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\n\nmyset.remove(\"banana\")\n\nprint(myset)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">discard()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>discard()</code> also removes a specified element, but it does not raise an error if\n    the element does not exist.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>myset = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\n\nmyset.discard(\"banana\")\n\nprint(myset)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">pop()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>pop()</code> removes and returns an element from the set. Because sets are unordered,\n    you should not rely on which element is removed.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>myset = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\n\nremoved = myset.pop()\n\nprint(removed)\nprint(myset)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">clear()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>clear()</code> removes every element from the set but leaves the set object itself.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>myset = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\n\nmyset.clear()\n\nprint(myset)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">del</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>del</code> keyword can delete the entire set.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>myset = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\n\ndel myset</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Loop Sets</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Use a <code>for</code> loop to process each item in a set.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>myset = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\n\nfor x in myset:\nprint(x)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-950/40 border-l-4 border-amber-500 text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Remember:\n    </strong>\n    The loop visits every item, but you should not assume the order in which set items will be returned.\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Join Sets</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-3 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Python provides several set operations for combining and comparing sets.\n</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Union</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>union()</code> method returns a new set containing all elements from both sets.\n    Duplicate values appear only once.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>set1 = {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"}\nset2 = {1, 2, 3}\n\nset3 = set1.union(set2)\n\nprint(set3)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>|</code> operator can also be used for union.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>set1 = {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"}\nset2 = {1, 2, 3}\n\nset3 = set1 | set2\n\nprint(set3)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Join Multiple Sets</h3>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>set1 = {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"}\nset2 = {1, 2, 3}\nset3 = {\"John\", \"Elena\"}\nset4 = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\n\nresult = set1.union(set2, set3, set4)\n\nprint(result)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Update with Union</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Unlike <code>union()</code>, <code>update()</code> modifies the existing set instead of returning\n    a separate combined set.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>set1 = {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"}\nset2 = {1, 2, 3}\n\nset1.update(set2)\n\nprint(set1)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Intersection</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Intersection keeps only the values that exist in both sets.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>set1 = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\nset2 = {\"google\", \"microsoft\", \"apple\"}\n\nresult = set1.intersection(set2)\n\nprint(result)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>&amp;</code> operator provides a shortcut for intersection.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>set1 = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\nset2 = {\"google\", \"microsoft\", \"apple\"}\n\nresult = set1 & set2\n\nprint(result)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">intersection_update()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>intersection_update()</code> changes the original set so that only common values remain.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>set1 = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\nset2 = {\"google\", \"microsoft\", \"apple\"}\n\nset1.intersection_update(set2)\n\nprint(set1)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Difference</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Difference returns values that are in the first set but not in the other set.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>set1 = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\nset2 = {\"google\", \"microsoft\", \"apple\"}\n\nresult = set1.difference(set2)\n\nprint(result)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>-</code> operator can be used as a shortcut.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>set1 = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\nset2 = {\"google\", \"microsoft\", \"apple\"}\n\nresult = set1 - set2\n\nprint(result)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">difference_update()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>difference_update()</code> removes from the original set every item that also appears\n    in the specified set.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>set1 = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\nset2 = {\"google\", \"microsoft\", \"apple\"}\n\nset1.difference_update(set2)\n\nprint(set1)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Symmetric Difference</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Symmetric difference keeps the values that appear in either set, but removes values that\n    appear in both.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>set1 = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\nset2 = {\"google\", \"microsoft\", \"apple\"}\n\nresult = set1.symmetric_difference(set2)\n\nprint(result)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>^</code> operator can be used as a shortcut.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>set1 = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\nset2 = {\"google\", \"microsoft\", \"apple\"}\n\nresult = set1 ^ set2\n\nprint(result)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">symmetric_difference_update()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    This method modifies the original set so it contains the symmetric difference.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>set1 = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\nset2 = {\"google\", \"microsoft\", \"apple\"}\n\nset1.symmetric_difference_update(set2)\n\nprint(set1)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Subset and Superset</h2>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">issubset()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>issubset()</code> returns <code>True</code> when every item in one set is also contained\n    in another set.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>x = {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"}\ny = {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\", \"e\"}\n\nprint(x.issubset(y))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>&lt;=</code> operator can be used as a subset shortcut.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>x = {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"}\ny = {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\", \"e\"}\n\nprint(x <= y)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Proper Subset</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>&lt;</code> operator checks for a proper subset, meaning the first set is a subset\n    but the two sets are not equal.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>x = {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"}\ny = {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\"}\n\nprint(x < y)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">issuperset()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>issuperset()</code> returns <code>True</code> when the current set contains every item\n    from the other set.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>x = {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\", \"e\"}\ny = {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"}\n\nprint(x.issuperset(y))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>&gt;=</code> operator is a superset shortcut.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>x = {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\", \"e\"}\ny = {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"}\n\nprint(x >= y)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Proper Superset</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>&gt;</code> operator checks for a proper superset, meaning the first set contains\n    the second set and has at least one additional item.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>x = {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\"}\ny = {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"}\n\nprint(x > y)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">isdisjoint()</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>isdisjoint()</code> returns <code>True</code> when two sets have no elements in common.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>x = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\ny = {\"google\", \"microsoft\", \"facebook\"}\n\nprint(x.isdisjoint(y))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Copy a Set</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Use <code>copy()</code> to create a separate copy of a set.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>set1 = {\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"}\n\nset2 = set1.copy()\n\nprint(set2)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Frozenset</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A <code>frozenset</code> is an immutable version of a set. It contains unique,\n    unordered elements, but you cannot add or remove elements after it has been created.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>x = frozenset({\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"})\n\nprint(x)\nprint(type(x))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A frozenset supports non-mutating set operations such as union, intersection,\n    difference, symmetric difference, and subset/superset checks.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-rose-50 dark:bg-rose-950/40 border-l-4 border-rose-500 text-rose-900 dark:text-rose-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation\"></i> Important:\n    </strong>\n    Unlike a normal set, a frozenset cannot use methods that add or remove elements.\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Set Methods Reference</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-3 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    These are the built-in set methods listed by W3Schools.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n    <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse\">\n        <thead>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-700\">\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Method</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Shortcut</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Purpose</th>\n            </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>add()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">—</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Adds an element</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>clear()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">—</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Removes all elements</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>copy()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">—</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Returns a copy</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>difference()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>-</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Returns the difference between sets</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>difference_update()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>-=</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Removes common elements from the current set</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>discard()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">—</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Removes a specified element without raising an error if absent</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>intersection()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>&amp;</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Returns elements common to the sets</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>intersection_update()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>&amp;=</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Keeps only common elements in the current set</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>isdisjoint()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">—</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Checks whether sets have no common elements</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>issubset()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>&lt;=</code> / <code>&lt;</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Checks whether all elements exist in another set</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>issuperset()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>&gt;=</code> / <code>&gt;</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Checks whether another set is contained in this set</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>pop()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">—</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Removes and returns an element</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>remove()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">—</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Removes a specified element</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>symmetric_difference()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>^</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Returns elements that are not common to both sets</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>symmetric_difference_update()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>^=</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Updates the current set with the symmetric difference</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>union()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>|</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Returns the union of sets</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>update()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>|=</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Updates a set with elements from another iterable</td>\n            </tr>\n        </tbody>\n    </table>\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Set Operations at a Glance</h2>\n\n<div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n    <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse\">\n        <thead>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-700\">\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Operation</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Method</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Operator</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Result</th>\n            </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Union</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>union()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>|</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">All unique items from both</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Intersection</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>intersection()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>&amp;</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Items common to both</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Difference</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>difference()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>-</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Items in the first but not the second</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Symmetric difference</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>symmetric_difference()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>^</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Items in either set, but not both</td>\n            </tr>\n        </tbody>\n    </table>\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Sets and Cybersecurity</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Sets are particularly useful when you need unique values or need to compare collections.\n    In cybersecurity programming, this can be useful for comparing IP addresses, ports,\n    usernames, domains, file names, permissions, or other groups of data.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>known_ips = {\"192.168.1.10\", \"192.168.1.20\", \"192.168.1.30\"}\nnew_ips = {\"192.168.1.20\", \"192.168.1.40\"}\n\nnew_addresses = new_ips.difference(known_ips)\n\nprint(new_addresses)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-shield-halved\"></i> Cybersecurity Connection:\n    </strong>\n    Set operations can make comparisons between collections very straightforward.\n    For example, <code>difference()</code> can identify values that appear in one collection\n    but not another.\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Set vs List vs Tuple</h2>\n\n<div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n    <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse\">\n        <thead>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-700\">\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Property</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">List</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Tuple</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Set</th>\n            </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Ordered</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Yes</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Yes</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">No</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Changeable</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Yes</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">No</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Items cannot be changed</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Indexed</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Yes</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Yes</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">No</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Duplicates</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Allowed</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Allowed</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Not allowed</td>\n            </tr>\n        </tbody>\n    </table>\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Quick Reference</h2>\n\n<div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n    <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse\">\n        <thead>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-700\">\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Task</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Python</th>\n            </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Create</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>myset = {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"}</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Length</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>len(myset)</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Check type</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>type(myset)</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Check membership</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>x in myset</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Add one</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>myset.add(x)</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Add many</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>myset.update(other)</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Remove safely</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>myset.discard(x)</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Remove with error if absent</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>myset.remove(x)</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Union</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>a | b</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Intersection</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>a &amp; b</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Difference</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>a - b</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Symmetric difference</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>a ^ b</code></td>\n            </tr>\n        </tbody>\n    </table>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 border-l-4 border-slate-500 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold\">Key takeaway:</strong>\n    Use a set when you need a collection of unique values and do not need to access items\n    by position. The most important set operations to understand are\n    <code>union()</code>, <code>intersection()</code>, <code>difference()</code>,\n    and <code>symmetric_difference()</code>.\n</div>\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "topic-1790009051951",
    "category": "Python Basics",
    "title": "Dictionaries",
    "content": "<p class=\"text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Dictionaries are used to store data in <strong>key:value</strong> pairs. A dictionary is\n    ordered in modern Python, is changeable, and does not allow duplicate keys.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>person = {\n    \"name\": \"John\",\n    \"age\": 36,\n    \"country\": \"UK\"\n}\n\nprint(person)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Key Idea:\n    </strong>\n    A dictionary maps a key to a value. Instead of using a numerical index like a list,\n    you normally use the key to access the value.\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Dictionary Items</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Dictionary items are written as <code>key: value</code> pairs inside curly brackets.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\",\n    \"year\": 1964\n}\n\nprint(car[\"brand\"])</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Ordered Dictionaries</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Python dictionaries preserve insertion order. This has been guaranteed since Python 3.7.\n    Earlier Python versions did not guarantee dictionary ordering.\n</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Changeable Dictionaries</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Dictionary entries can be changed, added, and removed after the dictionary is created.\n</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Duplicate Keys</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Dictionary keys must be unique. If the same key appears more than once, the later value\n    replaces the earlier value.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\",\n    \"year\": 1964,\n    \"year\": 2020\n}\n\nprint(car)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Dictionary Length</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Use <code>len()</code> to find the number of key:value pairs in a dictionary.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>person = {\n    \"name\": \"John\",\n    \"age\": 36,\n    \"country\": \"UK\"\n}\n\nprint(len(person))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Dictionary Value Data Types</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Dictionary values can contain any Python data type.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>person = {\n    \"name\": \"John\",\n    \"age\": 36,\n    \"is_student\": False,\n    \"skills\": [\"Python\", \"Linux\", \"Networking\"]\n}\n\nprint(person)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    This means dictionaries can contain strings, integers, Booleans, lists, tuples,\n    other dictionaries, and many other Python objects as values.\n</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">The type() Function</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Use <code>type()</code> to check the data type of a dictionary.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>person = {\n    \"name\": \"John\",\n    \"age\": 36\n}\n\nprint(type(person))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">The dict() Constructor</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A dictionary can also be created using the <code>dict()</code> constructor.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>person = dict(name=\"John\", age=36, country=\"UK\")\n\nprint(person)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Access Dictionary Items</h2>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Using Square Brackets</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Access a dictionary value by placing its key inside square brackets.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\",\n    \"year\": 1964\n}\n\nprint(car[\"model\"])</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Using get()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>get()</code> method can also retrieve a value from a key.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\",\n    \"year\": 1964\n}\n\nprint(car.get(\"model\"))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    You can provide a default value to <code>get()</code> if the key does not exist.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\"\n}\n\nprint(car.get(\"color\", \"Unknown\"))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-950/40 border-l-4 border-amber-500 text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\">\n        <i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Useful:\n    </strong>\n    <code>get()</code> is useful when a key may not exist and you want to supply a fallback value\n    rather than immediately raising a <code>KeyError</code>.\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Get Dictionary Keys</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>keys()</code> method returns a view containing the dictionary's keys.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\",\n    \"year\": 1964\n}\n\nx = car.keys()\n\nprint(x)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The keys view reflects later changes made to the dictionary.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\"\n}\n\nx = car.keys()\n\nprint(x)\n\ncar[\"color\"] = \"white\"\n\nprint(x)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Get Dictionary Values</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>values()</code> method returns a view containing the dictionary's values.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\",\n    \"year\": 1964\n}\n\nx = car.values()\n\nprint(x)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The values view also reflects changes to the original dictionary.\n</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Get Key-Value Pairs</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>items()</code> method returns a view containing the dictionary's key-value pairs.\n    Each pair is represented as a tuple.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\",\n    \"year\": 1964\n}\n\nx = car.items()\n\nprint(x)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The items view reflects changes made to the original dictionary.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-700 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\"\n}\n\nx = car.items()\n\ncar[\"year\"] = 2020\ncar[\"color\"] = \"red\"\n\nprint(x)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Check if a Key Exists</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Use the <code>in</code> keyword to check whether a key exists in a dictionary.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\",\n    \"year\": 1964\n}\n\nif \"model\" in car:\nprint(\"The model key exists.\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">not in</h3>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\"\n}\n\nif \"color\" not in car:\nprint(\"Color is not a key.\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Change Dictionary Items</h2>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Change a Value</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Assign a new value to an existing key to change its value.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\",\n    \"year\": 1964\n}\n\ncar[\"year\"] = 2020\n\nprint(car)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Update a Value with update()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>update()</code> method can change one or more key-value pairs.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\",\n    \"year\": 1964\n}\n\ncar.update({\"year\": 2020})\n\nprint(car)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Add Dictionary Items</h2>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Add Using a New Key</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Assigning a value to a key that does not yet exist adds a new item.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\",\n    \"year\": 1964\n}\n\ncar[\"color\"] = \"red\"\n\nprint(car)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Add with update()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>update()</code> can also add new key-value pairs when the keys do not already exist.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\"\n}\n\ncar.update({\"color\": \"red\"})\n\nprint(car)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Remove Dictionary Items</h2>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">pop()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>pop()</code> removes the item with a specified key and returns its value.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\",\n    \"year\": 1964\n}\n\nremoved = car.pop(\"model\")\n\nprint(removed)\nprint(car)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A default value can be supplied to <code>pop()</code> when the key might not exist.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\"\n}\n\nprint(car.pop(\"model\", \"Not found\"))</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">popitem()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>popitem()</code> removes and returns the last inserted key-value pair.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\",\n    \"year\": 1964\n}\n\nitem = car.popitem()\n\nprint(item)\nprint(car)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">del</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>del</code> keyword can remove a dictionary item by key.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\",\n    \"year\": 1964\n}\n\ndel car[\"model\"]\n\nprint(car)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>del</code> can also delete the entire dictionary.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\"\n}\n\ndel car</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">clear()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>clear()</code> removes all items while leaving the dictionary itself available.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\"\n}\n\ncar.clear()\n\nprint(car)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Loop Through a Dictionary</h2>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Loop Through Keys</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A <code>for</code> loop over a dictionary returns its keys by default.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\",\n    \"year\": 1964\n}\n\nfor key in car:\nprint(key)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Loop Through Values</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Use <code>values()</code> when you want to loop through only the values.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>car = {\n    \"brand\": \"Ford\",\n    \"model\": \"Mustang\",\n    \"year\": 1964\n}\n\nfor value in car.values():\nprint(value)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Loop Through Keys with keys()</h3>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>for key in car.keys():\n    print(key)</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Loop Through Key-Value Pairs</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Use <code>items()</code> to loop through keys and values together.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>for key, value in car.items():\n    print(key, value)</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Copy Dictionaries</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Assigning one dictionary variable directly to another does not create an independent copy.\n    Both variables refer to the same dictionary object.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>dict1 = {\n    \"name\": \"John\",\n    \"age\": 36\n}\n\ndict2 = dict1\n\ndict1[\"age\"] = 40\n\nprint(dict2)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">copy()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>copy()</code> method creates a separate shallow copy of the dictionary.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>dict1 = {\n    \"name\": \"John\",\n    \"age\": 36\n}\n\ndict2 = dict1.copy()\n\nprint(dict2)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">dict()</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    The <code>dict()</code> constructor can also create a copy.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>dict1 = {\n    \"name\": \"John\",\n    \"age\": 36\n}\n\ndict2 = dict(dict1)\n\nprint(dict2)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Nested Dictionaries</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A nested dictionary is a dictionary that contains one or more dictionaries as values.\n    This is useful for representing structured data.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>students = {\n    \"student1\": {\n        \"name\": \"John\",\n        \"age\": 15\n    },\n    \"student2\": {\n        \"name\": \"Sarah\",\n        \"age\": 16\n    },\n    \"student3\": {\n        \"name\": \"Michael\",\n        \"age\": 15\n    }\n}\n\nprint(students)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Access Nested Data</h3>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>print(students[\"student1\"][\"name\"])\nprint(students[\"student2\"][\"age\"])</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-2\">Creating Nested Dictionaries with a Loop</h3>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Nested dictionaries can also be generated programmatically.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>students = {}\n\nfor i in range(1, 4):\nstudents[f\"student{i}\"] = {\n\"name\": f\"Student {i}\",\n\"age\": 15 + i\n}\n\nprint(students)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Dictionary Methods</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-3 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Python provides built-in methods for working with dictionaries.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n    <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse\">\n        <thead>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-700\">\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Method</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Purpose</th>\n            </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>clear()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Removes all items from the dictionary.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>copy()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Returns a copy of the dictionary.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>fromkeys()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Creates a dictionary using specified keys and a common value.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>get()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Returns the value associated with a key.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>items()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Returns a view of key-value pairs.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>keys()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Returns a view of the dictionary's keys.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>pop()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Removes the item with a specified key.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>popitem()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Removes the last inserted key-value pair.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>setdefault()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Returns a value and inserts the key if it does not exist.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>update()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Updates the dictionary with key-value pairs.</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>values()</code></td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Returns a view of all values.</td>\n            </tr>\n        </tbody>\n    </table>\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">fromkeys()</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>fromkeys()</code> creates a dictionary using a sequence of keys and one value\n    that is assigned to each key.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>keys = (\"name\", \"age\", \"country\")\n\nperson = dict.fromkeys(keys)\n\nprint(person)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A default value can also be supplied.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>keys = (\"name\", \"age\", \"country\")\n\nperson = dict.fromkeys(keys, \"unknown\")\n\nprint(person)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">setdefault()</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    <code>setdefault()</code> returns the value of a specified key.\n    If the key does not exist, it inserts the key using the supplied default value.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>person = {\n    \"name\": \"John\",\n    \"age\": 36\n}\n\ncountry = person.setdefault(\"country\", \"UK\")\n\nprint(country)\nprint(person)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Dictionary Methods in Practice</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    A dictionary can combine several methods to process structured information.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>user = {\n    \"username\": \"michael\",\n    \"role\": \"student\",\n    \"active\": True\n}\n\nprint(user.get(\"username\"))\n\nfor key, value in user.items():\nprint(key, \"=\", value)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Dictionaries and Cybersecurity</h2>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Dictionaries are particularly useful in cybersecurity because structured information often\n    consists of named fields. For example, a security event can contain an IP address,\n    username, timestamp, event type, and status.\n</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3 group\">\n    <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\">\n        <i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy\n    </button>\n    <pre><code>event = {\n    \"ip\": \"192.168.1.25\",\n    \"username\": \"admin\",\n    \"port\": 22,\n    \"status\": \"failed\",\n    \"attempts\": 3\n}\n\nprint(event[\"ip\"])\nprint(event[\"status\"])</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"mb-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300\">\n    Dictionaries are also commonly used for representing parsed JSON data and configuration data.\n</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Dictionary vs Other Collections</h2>\n\n<div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n    <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse\">\n        <thead>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-700\">\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Property</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">List</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Tuple</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Set</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Dictionary</th>\n            </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Ordered</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Yes</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Yes</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">No</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Yes</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Changeable</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Yes</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">No</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Yes</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Yes</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Duplicates</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Allowed</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Allowed</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Not allowed</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Duplicate keys not allowed</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Access</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Index</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Index</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Membership</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Key</td>\n            </tr>\n        </tbody>\n    </table>\n</div>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6 mb-3\">Quick Reference</h2>\n\n<div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n    <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse\">\n        <thead>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-700\">\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Task</th>\n                <th class=\"text-left py-2 px-3\">Python</th>\n            </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Create</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>person = {\"name\": \"John\"}</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Access</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>person[\"name\"]</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Safe access</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>person.get(\"name\")</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Length</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>len(person)</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Get keys</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>person.keys()</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Get values</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>person.values()</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Get pairs</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>person.items()</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Check key</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>\"name\" in person</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Change</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>person[\"age\"] = 16</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Add</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>person[\"country\"] = \"UK\"</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Remove</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>person.pop(\"age\")</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Loop keys</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>for key in person:</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Loop values</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>for value in person.values():</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Loop pairs</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>for key, value in person.items():</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800\">\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Copy</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>person.copy()</code></td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\">Clear</td>\n                <td class=\"py-2 px-3\"><code>person.clear()</code></td>\n            </tr>\n        </tbody>\n    </table>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 border-l-4 border-slate-500 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200 text-sm\">\n    <strong class=\"font-bold\">Key takeaway:</strong>\n    Dictionaries store information using key-value pairs. The most important skills are\n    creating dictionaries, accessing values by key, changing and adding items, removing items,\n    looping through keys and values, copying dictionaries, and working with nested dictionaries\n    and dictionary methods.\n</div>\n"
  },
