    "id": "topic-1790009102348",
    "category": "Python Basics",
    "title": "If else",
    "content": "<h1>Python If...Else</h1>\n\n<p>Python uses <code>if</code>, <code>elif</code>, and <code>else</code> statements to make decisions in your programs.</p>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n  <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Tip:</strong>\n  If statements allow your program to choose what code to run depending on whether a condition is <code>True</code> or <code>False</code>.\n</div>\n\n<h2>Python Conditions</h2>\n\n<p>Python uses comparison operators to create conditions.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>==    # Equal to\n!=    # Not equal to\n&gt;     # Greater than\n&lt;     # Less than\n&gt;=    # Greater than or equal to\n&lt;=    # Less than or equal to</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<p>Example:</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>age = 18\n\nif age >= 18:\n print(\"You are an adult\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n  <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Tip:</strong>\n  A condition evaluates to either <code>True</code> or <code>False</code>.\n</div>\n\n<h2>The if Statement</h2>\n\n<p>The <code>if</code> statement runs a block of code when its condition is <code>True</code>.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>x = 10\n\nif x > 5:\n print(\"x is greater than 5\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p>If the condition is <code>False</code>, the code inside the <code>if</code> statement will not run.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>x = 3\n\nif x > 5:\nprint(\"x is greater than 5\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p>There is no output because <code>3 &gt; 5</code> is <code>False</code>.</p>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n  <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Tip:</strong>\n  The colon <code>:</code> starts the block of code that belongs to the <code>if</code> statement.\n</div>\n\n<h2>Indentation</h2>\n\n<p>Python uses indentation to define which statements belong to an <code>if</code> block.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>if 10 &gt; 5:\n    print(\"10 is greater than 5\")</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<p>The indentation is required.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>if 10 &gt; 5:\nprint(\"10 is greater than 5\")</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<p>The example above causes an error because the <code>print()</code> statement is not indented.</p>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n  <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Tip:</strong>\n  Python normally uses four spaces for indentation.\n</div>\n\n<h2>The elif Statement</h2>\n\n<p>The <code>elif</code> statement means \"else if\". It lets you check another condition when the previous condition is <code>False</code>.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>age = 16\n\nif age >= 18:\n print(\"Adult\")\nelif age >= 13:\n print(\"Teenager\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p>You can use multiple <code>elif</code> statements.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>score = 75\n\nif score >= 90:\n print(\"Grade A\")\nelif score >= 80:\n print(\"Grade B\")\nelif score >= 70:\n print(\"Grade C\")\nelif score >= 60:\n print(\"Grade D\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n  <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Tip:</strong>\n  Python checks conditions from top to bottom and runs the first block whose condition is <code>True</code>.\n</div>\n\n<h2>The else Statement</h2>\n\n<p>The <code>else</code> statement runs when all previous conditions are <code>False</code>.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>age = 12\n\nif age >= 18:\n print(\"Adult\")\nelse:\n print(\"Not an adult\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p>The <code>else</code> statement does not need a condition.</p>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n  <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Tip:</strong>\n  Think of <code>else</code> as the \"otherwise\" part of a decision.\n</div>\n\n<h2>if...elif...else</h2>\n\n<p>You can combine <code>if</code>, <code>elif</code>, and <code>else</code> to handle several possibilities.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>age = 20\n\nif age < 13:\n print(\"Child\")\nelif age < 18:\n print(\"Teenager\")\nelse:\n print(\"Adult\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p>The general structure is:</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>if condition:\n    # code\nelif another_condition:\n    # code\nelse:\n    # code</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Multiple Conditions</h2>\n\n<p>You can use logical operators to combine conditions.</p>\n\n<p>The three main logical operators are:</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>and\nor\nnot</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<h3>The and Operator</h3>\n\n<p>The <code>and</code> operator requires both conditions to be <code>True</code>.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>age = 20\nhas_id = True\n\nif age >= 18 and has_id:\n print(\"You can enter\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n  <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Tip:</strong>\n  With <code>and</code>, every condition must be <code>True</code>.\n</div>\n\n<h3>The or Operator</h3>\n\n<p>The <code>or</code> operator is <code>True</code> when at least one condition is <code>True</code>.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>day = \"Saturday\"\n\nif day == \"Saturday\" or day == \"Sunday\":\n print(\"It is the weekend\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h3>The not Operator</h3>\n\n<p>The <code>not</code> operator reverses the result of a condition.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>is_raining = False\n\nif not is_raining:\n print(\"You do not need an umbrella\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n  <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Tip:</strong>\n  <code>not True</code> becomes <code>False</code>, while <code>not False</code> becomes <code>True</code>.\n</div>\n\n<h2>Nested if Statements</h2>\n\n<p>An <code>if</code> statement can be placed inside another <code>if</code> statement. This is called a nested <code>if</code>.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>age = 20\nhas_id = True\n\nif age >= 18:\n if has_id:\n  print(\"You can enter\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p>A nested <code>if</code> can also contain an <code>else</code> statement.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>age = 20\nhas_id = False\n\nif age >= 18:\n if has_id:\n  print(\"You can enter\")\n else:\n print(\"You need identification\")\nelse:\n print(\"You are too young\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n  <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Tip:</strong>\n  Avoid deeply nested <code>if</code> statements when possible. Logical operators can sometimes make your code easier to read.\n</div>\n\n<h2>Short Hand if</h2>\n\n<p>If you only need one statement, you can place the entire <code>if</code> statement on one line.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>if 10 &gt; 5: print(\"10 is greater than 5\")</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Short Hand if...else</h2>\n\n<p>You can also write an <code>if...else</code> statement on one line.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>age = 20\n\nprint(\"Adult\") if age >= 18 else print(\"Minor\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p>This is called a conditional expression.</p>\n\n<p>You can also use it to assign a value:</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>age = 20\n\nstatus = \"Adult\" if age >= 18 else \"Minor\"\n\nprint(status)</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n  <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Tip:</strong>\n  One-line <code>if</code> statements are useful for simple conditions, but normal multi-line statements are often easier to read.\n</div>\n\n<h2>The pass Statement</h2>\n\n<p>An <code>if</code> statement cannot be empty. Use <code>pass</code> when you want the block to do nothing.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>age = 18\n\nif age >= 18:\n pass</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n  <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Tip:</strong>\n  <code>pass</code> is often used as a placeholder while developing a program.\n</div>\n\n<h2>if...else with User Input</h2>\n\n<p><code>if...else</code> statements are commonly used with <code>input()</code>.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>age = int(input(\"Enter your age: \"))\n\nif age >= 18:\n print(\"You are an adult\")\nelse:\n print(\"You are a minor\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p>The result depends on the number entered by the user.</p>\n\n<h2>Checking Strings</h2>\n\n<p>You can use <code>if</code> statements to compare strings.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>username = \"Michael\"\n\nif username == \"Michael\":\n print(\"Welcome Michael\")\nelse:\n print(\"Unknown user\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p>You can also check whether two strings are different using <code>!=</code>.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>password = \"hello123\"\n\nif password != \"admin\":\n print(\"Incorrect password\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2>The in Operator</h2>\n\n<p>The <code>in</code> operator checks whether a value exists inside a sequence such as a list or string.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"orange\"]\n\nif \"apple\" in fruits:\n print(\"Apple is in the list\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p>You can also use <code>not in</code>.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"orange\"]\n\nif \"grape\" not in fruits:\n print(\"Grape is not in the list\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2>Boolean Values</h2>\n\n<p>Boolean values can only be <code>True</code> or <code>False</code>.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>logged_in = True\n\nif logged_in:\n print(\"Welcome\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p>You can use <code>not</code> to check for the opposite value.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>logged_in = False\n\nif not logged_in:\n print(\"Please log in\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<h2>Example</h2>\n\n<p>Here is a simple grade calculator using <code>if</code>, <code>elif</code>, and <code>else</code>:</p>\n\n<div class=\"bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-xl relative my-3\">\n  <button onclick=\"copyCode(this)\" class=\"absolute top-2.5 right-2.5 px-2 py-1 text-xs bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 rounded border border-slate-700\"><i class=\"fa-regular fa-copy\"></i> Copy</button>\n  <pre><code>score = int(input(\"Enter your score: \"))\n\nif score >= 90:\n print(\"Grade A\")\nelif score >= 80:\n print(\"Grade B\")\nelif score >= 70:\n print(\"Grade C\")\nelif score >= 60:\n print(\"Grade D\")\nelse:\n print(\"Grade F\")</code></pre>\n\n</div>\n\n<p>Python checks each condition from top to bottom. Once it finds a condition that is <code>True</code>, it runs that block and skips the remaining conditions.</p>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n  <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Tip:</strong>\n  Put conditions in the correct order because Python stops checking once it finds a <code>True</code> condition.\n</div>\n\n<h2>Summary</h2>\n\n<div class=\"my-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 text-sm\">\n  <strong class=\"font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\"></i> Tip:</strong>\n  <code>if</code> checks a condition.<br>\n  <code>elif</code> checks another condition.<br>\n  <code>else</code> runs when previous conditions are <code>False</code>.<br>\n  <code>and</code> requires all conditions to be <code>True</code>.<br>\n  <code>or</code> requires at least one condition to be <code>True</code>.<br>\n  <code>not</code> reverses a condition.<br>\n  <code>in</code> checks whether a value exists in a sequence.<br>\n  <code>not in</code> checks whether a value does not exist in a sequence.<br>\n  Python uses indentation to define blocks of code.\n</div>\n"
